 AI Foundry by integrating evaluation tools with top governance platforms. These integrations allow you to define, execute, and monitor AI risk and compliance workflows seamlessly, without affecting developer productivity.",DescriptionFoundry:"Streamline AI governance with Microsoft Foundry by integrating evaluation tools with top governance platforms. These integrations allow you to define, execute, and monitor AI risk and compliance workflows seamlessly, without affecting developer productivity.",Title:"Governance"},Card2:{ButtonLabel:"Go to Purview",Description:"Assess and manage compliance for your AI apps with Microsoft Purview Compliance Manager. It translates AI regulations, such as the EU AI Act, into actionable suggestions that you can implement in Azure AI Foundry to run your AI evaluations. Upload the results back to Microsoft Purview Compliance Manager assessments for a comprehensive view of your regulatory posture, ensuring you stay current with regulations and certifications, and can report effectively to auditors.",DescriptionFoundry:"Assess and manage compliance for your AI apps with Microsoft Purview Compliance Manager. It translates AI regulations, such as the EU AI Act, into actionable suggestions that you can implement in Microsoft Foundry to run your AI evaluations. Upload the results back to Microsoft Purview Compliance Manager assessments for a comprehensive view of your regulatory posture, ensuring you stay current with regulations and certifications, and can report effectively to auditors.",LinkLabel:"Learn more",Title:"Microsoft Purview"},Card3:{ButtonLabel:"Go to Credo AI",Description:"Define evaluation requirements for AI projects with the Credo AI integration for Azure AI Foundry. Governance teams can set project-specific and compliance-based requirements, which are then converted into executable code for developers to run Evaluators directly in Foundry. This closed-loop approach removes traditional bottlenecks and ensures AI systems meet compliance standards from the start.",DescriptionFoundry:"Define evaluation requirements for AI projects with the Credo AI integration for Microsoft Foundry. Governance teams can set project-specific and compliance-based requirements, which are then converted into executable code for developers to run Evaluators directly in Foundry. This closed-loop approach removes traditional bottlenecks and ensures AI systems meet compliance standards from the start.",LinkLabel:"Learn more",Title:"Credo AI integration"},Card4:{ButtonLabel:"Get Saidot",Description:"Connect your Azure model registry to govern AI models and agents in Saidot with the Microsoft Azure AI Foundry integration. Generate evaluation plans based on risk profiles, including red teaming and simulated datasets. Run evaluations in Azure, review results in Saidot, and report to risk and compliance—all in one streamlined workflow.",DescriptionFoundry:"Connect your Azure model registry to govern AI models and agents in Saidot with the Microsoft Foundry integration. Generate evaluation plans based on risk profiles, including red teaming and simulated datasets. Run evaluations in Azure, review results in Saidot, and report to risk and compliance—all in one streamlined workflow.",LinkLabel:"Learn more",Title:"Saidot integration"},Card5:{ButtonLabel:"View Apps",Description:"Foundry system-assigned managed identities are now automatically labeled as Microsoft Entra Agent IDs.",DescriptionFoundry:"Microsoft Foundry system-assigned managed identities are now automatically labeled as Microsoft Entra Agent IDs.",LinkLabel:"Learn more",Title:"Microsoft Entra"},ComingSoon:"Coming Soon",PageTitle:"AI development with a governance-first approach"},ia={Governance:s4};let Qg=ia;const a4={[m.En]:()=>Promise.resolve(ia),[m.QpsPloc]:()=>Promise.resolve(Ge.pseudolocalizeStrings(ia)),[m.Es]:()=>c(()=>__aml_import(()=>import("./en-us.es-48a5ad9b.js")),[]),[m.Cs]:()=>c(()=>__aml_import(()=>import("./en-us.cs-c22f474d.js")),[]),[m.De]: